# Relativiskick

## Background

A black hole created by CERN has flung you into outer space, where the civilization of Sirius has taken you to compete in an interstellar soccer match. What makes interstellar soccer unique is its enormous scale, which means that relativistic effects must be taken into account. The match consists of two halves. In the first half, Tactical Replication and Tactical Analysis will test your technical skills as well as your knowledge of physics and mathematics. In the second half, you must design and execute different tactics against a variety of defensive formations. Your ultimate goal is to break through the Sirius defense and score.

